This grant applies to personal, educational, research, nonprofit, and commercial applications.

### 2. Authorized Derivative Distributions

Licensees may create and distribute derivative versions of Dualscan OS, including customized operating system images, device-specific builds, and commercial OEM distributions.

Permitted customization includes:

- Adding proprietary or open-source applications.
- Adding custom interfaces, themes, and branding.
- Integrating additional hardware and software functionality.
- Modifying non-protected system components.
- Distributing customized images commercially without payment of licensing royalties.

### 3. Mandatory Preservation of Core OEM Components

Every redistributed or derivative Dualscan OS image must preserve the Core OEM Components supplied in the original licensed distribution.

Core OEM Components include the applications, configurations, system services, and home-screen tray applications expressly identified in the Licensor's published Core OEM Component Manifest.

Licensees shall not remove, disable, replace, conceal, or materially impair these components in distributed derivatives without prior written authorization.

### 4. Home-Screen Tray Preservation

All mandatory Dualscan OS OEM applications originally designated for the home-screen tray must remain installed, accessible, and visibly represented in their designated tray positions in every redistributed derivative.

Licensees may add applications or additional launchers, provided that such modifications do not remove, conceal, or interfere with the mandatory OEM tray applications.

### 5. Operational Integrity

Additional applications, services, and customizations must not intentionally interfere with the intended operation of the protected Dualscan OS OEM applications.

This requirement applies to derivative distributions as delivered and does not prohibit ordinary end-user control over a lawfully acquired device.

